SUMMARY:Sandy Hook Birding
DESCRIPTION:November can be excellent for migratory waterbirds\, raptors\, and late fall songbirds at this coastal hotspot. Arriving waterfowl and lingering land birds at one of the state’s best hotspots. We’ll scan the ocean and bay for migrating seafowl and work the hook’s thickets and woods for sparrows and other songbirds.Bring lunch and be prepared for walking over flat and sandy terrain. Led by Scott Barnes and associate naturalists. \nLocation: Meet at Parking Lot B\, about halfway down the lot by the bathrooms \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/sandy-hook-birding-34/
LOCATION:Sandy Hook – Lot B\, Hartshorne Drive\, Sandy Hook\, NJ\, 07732\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sandy-Hook-Birding-11.2026.webp
GEO:40.4071808233;-73.9782969352
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Sandy Hook – Lot B Hartshorne Drive Sandy Hook NJ 07732 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=Hartshorne Drive:geo:-73.9782969352,40.4071808233
END:VEVENT
